# data-models-relationships

## Core Data Models

### Treatment Facilities
- Dual categorization system: treatment centers and sober living facilities
- Verification status tracking with multi-step approval workflow
- Provider network affiliations and insurance acceptance patterns
- Geographic service area boundaries and coverage mapping
- Specialty service flagging (detox, residential, outpatient)
Importance Score: 85

### Legal Cases
- Case type classification for custody reunification and expungement
- Document requirements mapped to case milestones
- Auto-generated legal document templates by case type
- Custom milestone sequencing for different legal processes
Importance Score: 90

### Community Resources
- Multi-category resource classification (housing, food, medical)
- Verification status tracking for community-submitted resources
- Service eligibility criteria mapping
- Geographic coverage area definition
Importance Score: 80

## Relationships

### Provider Networks
- Treatment facility network memberships
- Insurance acceptance relationships
- Service area overlaps
- Referral pathway tracking
Importance Score: 75

### Resource Verification
- Community-driven verification workflow
- Multi-step approval process
- User role-based verification permissions
- Verification history tracking
Importance Score: 85

### Service Availability
- Resource capacity tracking
- Service scheduling relationships
- Eligibility criteria mapping
- Population-specific service matching
Importance Score: 70

